[[0,524955,0,12,0,12,"2015-09-19T14:26:14","lllllllllll","",[],"","Croatia will \"force\" Hungary to accept migrants by continuing to send them to Hungary's border, its PM says.","http://www.bbc.com/news/world-europe-34302285","forefront"],[1,2501506,0,8,0,8,"2015-09-19T14:50:13","whynotanon1","[e]",[],"<p>Croatia is out of control. They claimed to be a safe transit country and were planning to welcome migrants, that lasted for exactly one day and then they became overwhelmed. They weren't prepared to handle them, no one is, so now they are putting them on buses and trains and forcing them into other countries. <strong>Croatia is engaging in state sponsored human trafficking.</strong> They've already sent trains loaded with migrants to Slovenia and Hungary. Hungary need to set up border controls ASAP between Croatia.</p>\n<p>These politicians have no idea what they are saying when they invite the migrants, like Germany and Croatia did. Hungary was playing the right move all along.</p>"],[2,2501744,2501506,5,0,5,"2015-09-19T15:15:53","Maxcactus","",[],"<p>These people are becoming a hot potatoes.</p>"],[1,2501660,0,6,0,6,"2015-09-19T15:07:41","daswalker","[e]",[],"<p>Fuck this. Hungary struggled with handling hundreds of thousands of immigrants for months and received close to no help from anyone. Certainly not from Croatia.</p>\n<p>When the government decided to close the borders, Croatia was the loudest about how inhuman it is, but how well they'll take care of the immigrants.</p>\n<p>That was, until their whole system collapsed under the weight of a few thousand immigrants in just ONE DAY. They pretty much went from &quot;we'll give our biggest love to all &lt;3&quot; to what Hungary reached in months, in just 24 hours. The only reason they are not closing their border is because that would make the immigrants go through a route that is full of landmines.</p>\n<p>And now, after spitting on Hungary for closing the borders for not being able to handle this whole thing alone, they are SNEAKING trains full of immigrants and ARMED policemen not only through Hungary's borders, but with that, also through the borders of the Schengen Area. AND, their comment on this is pretty much &quot;lol, we'll just keep doing this&quot;.</p>\n<p>I'll be curious what the EU's answer will be to that. At the least, I'm pretty sure they won't be allowed to join Schengen anytime soon.</p>\n<p>Also, Hungary started building a fence on the Croatian side too now because of this. Inside the EU. This whole thing is very fucked.</p>"]]
[]
[[0,524957,0,8,0,8,"2015-09-19T14:29:17","lllllllllll","",[],"","Live: AI bots try to fool human judges","http://www.bbc.com/news/live/technology-34281198","cuttingedge"],[1,2501413,0,1,0,1,"2015-09-19T14:35:47","Frenchgeek","",[],"<p>Let me guess : the winner will be a bot to warn us against the &quot;white genocide&quot;...</p>"],[2,2501669,2501413,2,0,2,"2015-09-19T15:08:05","Project2501","[A][e]",[],"<p>Eh ... a chat bot has already beaten human judges, by acting like a teenager. EDIT: <a href=\"http://www.theguardian.com/technology/2014/jun/08/super-computer-simulates-13-year-old-boy-passes-turing-test\">quick summary found through googling it</a>. </p>"],[3,2501809,2501669,2,0,2,"2015-09-19T15:22:24","Frenchgeek","",[],"<p>So the best way for a complex bot to pass as human is indeed to act like a simple one.</p>"],[4,2502182,2501809,2,0,2,"2015-09-19T16:01:08","Project2501","[A]",[],"<p>Pretty much. </p>"]]
